secubox-torrent (2.2.9-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * FIX conserved MP3/FLAC (and other common audio) went to PeerTube — a video
    platform — because secubox-torrent-conserve uploaded every conserved file
    through peertubectl regardless of type. It now classifies each file
    (extension-based; ambiguous .mkv is content-probed via ffprobe when
    available) and routes audio to Lyrion (`lyrionctl ingest`) while video
    keeps going to PeerTube unchanged. Destination per category is declarative
    — [conserve] video/audio in torrent.toml — not hardcoded. An unrecognised
    file type is never routed anywhere (terminal error, dequeued); an absent
    or unreachable Lyrion leaves the item queued for a later retry, exactly
    like the existing "peertubectl not installed" degrade path (ref #967).
  * Recommends: secubox-lyrion, ffmpeg (ffprobe resolves ambiguous containers).

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0200

secubox-torrent (2.2.8-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=high

  * FIX no download / 0 peers: throttleUpload(0) blocked the BitTorrent handshake
    and piece requests (both are "uploads"), so nothing ever connected. Removed
    the upload throttle + the ½-BW tuner (they also deadlocked: 0 download → 0
    upload → 0 download). Anti-seedbox is now purely structural — reapIdle unloads
    COMPLETE idle torrents (finished content stops seeding), while in-progress
    downloads keep normal upload (protocol works) and finish. TORRENT_SEED=full
    keeps completed torrents loaded (real seedbox).

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 19:35:00 +0200

secubox-torrent (2.2.7-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=high

  * FIX added torrents stuck at 0%%/never download: reapIdle unloaded INCOMPLETE
    torrents after 15min idle, killing in-progress downloads. Now only COMPLETE
    torrents are reaped — an unfinished download stays loaded to finish.

